ID: B3-Ch04a-Introduction
TEXT:

 I press the confirm key, and lines of Common text scroll onto the display. The screen is too small to hold the full briefing at once, requiring the side toggle to advance through the pages.

'Congratulations!' the text reads. 'Your auxiliary parameters are now operational. Please note that these three aura enhancements remain in the experimental trial phase. If you observe anomalous feedback, report the variance to your assigned technician. The following overview details each parameter's operational scope. Complete documentation is available in the user manual supplied with your unit.'

A user manual. It figures. A thousand years of lessathi engineering and I have to stumble through the hardware by trial and error while ancient operators had a booklet.

I click the toggle to load the first parameter.

'Magical Sense enhances passive and active aura analysis,' the display reads. 'Higher investment extends your detection radius and sharpens your perception of intricate flow currents and layered spell signatures. Operational efficacy scales with your baseline biological sensitivity. Subjects with faint natural auras may require higher point allocation to achieve comparable clarity.'

I click the toggle again.

'Aura Hardening reinforces personal defenses against offensive magical constructs,' the text explains. 'This parameter provides minimal resistance to physical kinetic force and must not replace Toughness or Reflexes. Trials confirm optimal dissipation against conventional elemental spells, alongside secondary mitigation against synthesized energy vectors including lightning, acid, and flash-frozen ice. Incoming non-magical projectiles retain standard mass and velocity; evasion remains mandatory.'

'Aura Hardening - Supplementary Notes: Field testers demonstrated offensive applications by concentrating hardened aura around their extremities to deflect incoming magical projectiles back toward the caster. Operational use outside laboratory conditions is strongly discouraged due to high failure rates in uncalibrated subjects.'

I click the toggle to bring up the final entry.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch04a-Introduction2, v_strength = 0, v_agility = 0, v_toughness = 0, v_reflexes = 0, v_hearing = 0, v_perception = 0, v_ancient_languages = 0, v_combat_technique = 0, v_premonition = 0, v_available_points = 25, v_current_scene = B3-Ch04a-Introduction2, v_b3_ch3_stats_unavailable = 0) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
