ID: B3-Ch04a-Introduction2
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch4_introduction == 1) {
 'The Bluff parameter, designated secondarily as Aura Concealment, governs aura modulation,' the text reads. 'Its primary function is stabilization. Sufficient investment dampens involuntary aura fluctuations, preventing detection by magical lie-sensing methods. Efficacy is tethered to innate aura control; subjects with erratic natural flow require higher point investment to stabilize the baseline.'

'Secondary utility was established during field testing,' the next page reads. 'While designed solely to mask deceptive fluctuations, trained subjects successfully suppressed their aura signatures entirely, rendering themselves invisible to standard magical detection. The hardware was subsequently recalibrated to support full suppression, and the parameter was given its secondary designation. If your unit fails to achieve complete dampening, consult your technical supervisor.'

}
#if(v_b3_ch4_introduction == 0 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 I press the skip key, clearing the tutorial prompt.

'Aura parameter briefing bypassed,' the display reads. 'You may review this documentation at any time in the operator manual provided with your unit. Advancing to the primary interface. Unspent points have been restored to your available pool following unit reset.'

A user manual from a thousand years ago. That would have saved me half a dozen near-death experiences.

I click the side button, and the familiar stat grid appears on the glass. The three new entries sit below the standard nine attributes, all resting at zero. I need to decide whether to allocate my points immediately or hold them in reserve.

}
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 && v_b3_ch4_introduction == 0) {
 I press the skip key, clearing the tutorial prompt.

'Aura parameter briefing bypassed,' the display reads. 'You may review this documentation at any time in the operator manual provided with your unit. Advancing to the primary interface. Unspent points have been restored to your available pool following unit reset.'

A user manual from a thousand years ago. That would have saved me half a dozen near-death experiences.

I click the side button, and the familiar stat grid appears on the glass. The three new attributes sit below the standard nine attributes, all resting at zero. In the corner, my pool displays an extra point—the advance Reidzek warned me about when my accidental lockout triggered early allocation. That means one less point when the next tier unlocks.

I need to decide whether to allocate my points immediately or hold them in reserve.

}
#if(v_b3_ch4_introduction == 1 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 I hit the toggle one last time to exit the manual.

'Briefing complete,' the screen confirms. 'Advancing to primary interface. Previously allocated points have been returned to your available reserve following system recalibration.'

The grid loads onto the glass, displaying the three new attributes below the original nine, all set to zero. I need to decide whether to assign my points now or hold them in reserve.

}
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 && v_b3_ch4_introduction == 1) {
 I hit the toggle one last time to exit the manual.

'Briefing complete,' the screen confirms. 'Advancing to primary interface. Previously allocated points have been returned to your available reserve following system recalibration.'

The grid loads onto the glass, displaying the three new attributes below the original nine, all set to zero. In the corner, my pool displays an extra point—the advance Reidzek warned me about when my accidental lockout triggered early allocation. That means one less point when the next tier unlocks. I need to decide whether to assign my points now or hold them in reserve.

}
